  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "VRChat Version:\n2021.3.1p1 - Build 1114\nDescription of the bug:\nHeavy lag (~2 second lag spikes every second) when there are more players in an instance than the soft cap.\nSteps to reproduce (how did you encounter the bug?):\n1. Join an instance(mostly encounter this bug in Furry Talk and Chill public instances)\n2. Wait until there are more players than the soft cap(20 for the above world)\n3. Lag\nAny extra files? (output logs, screenshots):\n1. Log:\nhttps://drive.google.com/file/d/1WBtSwFosPeyQudlyPkaaGGVHabK67_Km/view?usp=sharing\nLog file produced by a client with MelonLoader installed(no mods though).\nHowever, this bug occurs on vanilla client as well.\n2. Safety settings:\nOnly voice&icons for everyone except the trusted and friends.\nTrusted: everything except shaders/custom animations/sounds\nFriends: everything\n3. I haven't encountered a lot of people with the same issue, so I suspect this bug might have something to do with my setup.\nPC specs:\nCPU: Intel(R) Core(TM) i7 CPU         870  @ 2.93GHz\nGPU: GeForce GTX 1070 (Game Ready driver 471.11)\nRAM: 12 GB @ 1333 MHz\n4. Disabling the voice in safety settings for Visitor up to Known *seems* to help reduce the lag.",
